From 681266034eb8d9c13a6d8336ce006499ea704216 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vovij <ap22292@qmul.ac.uk>
Date: Fri, 5 Jun 2026 18:54:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/17] fix: resolve lr_scheduler param_group mismatch with
 DeepSpeed ZeRO-2

Problem:
Training crashed with ValueError: zip() argument 2 is longer/shorter
than argument 1 inside torch.optim.lr_scheduler._update_lr() at the
first optimizer step.

Root cause:
get_optimizer_grouped_parameters() returned 2 param groups (one with
weight decay for non-bias/norm params, one without for bias/norm params).
DeepSpeed ZeRO-2 internally merges these into a single param group during
deepspeed.initialize(). The lr_scheduler was built against the original
2-group optimizer, so scheduler.base_lrs had 2 entries while
optimizer.param_groups had 1. PyTorch scheduler uses
zip(self.base_lrs, self.optimizer.param_groups, strict=True) which
raised the mismatch error.

Fix:
Simplified get_optimizer_grouped_parameters() in deepspeed_utils.py
to return a single param group containing all trainable parameters.
This ensures the scheduler and optimizer always have a consistent param
group count before and after DeepSpeed initialization.

No other files were modified. deepspeed.py and train_sft.py remain
unchanged from the original.

Files changed:
- openrlhf/utils/deepspeed/deepspeed_utils.py
    - get_optimizer_grouped_parameters(): return 1 param group instead
      of 2 (decay vs no-decay split removed)

Note:
The weight decay distinction between bias/norm params and other params
is not needed here as all trainable parameters are LoRA adapter weights
and memory token embeddings which are trained uniformly.
